WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:03.019
(screaming)

00:00:03.019 --> 00:00:05.109
- [Narrator] When a big earthquake hits,

00:00:05.109 --> 00:00:08.609
collapsed buildings can bury people alive.

00:00:09.533 --> 00:00:10.612
- [Narrator] That's when the legendary

00:00:10.612 --> 00:00:13.529
human moles of Mexico City come in.

00:00:16.651 --> 00:00:17.990
- [Narrator] And when the moles arrive,

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:21.407
the community comes together as one fist.

00:00:41.809 --> 00:00:44.726
(mid-tempo music)

00:00:54.722 --> 00:00:57.059
- [Narrator] In 1985, Mexico City was hit

00:00:57.059 --> 00:00:58.932
by a devastating earthquake

00:00:58.932 --> 00:01:01.871
that killed roughly 10,000 people.

00:01:01.871 --> 00:01:03.812
That's when a group of volunteers decided

00:01:03.812 --> 00:01:07.979
to form a collective to
help fellow human beings.

00:01:56.784 --> 00:01:57.804
- [Narrator] The members of the Topos

00:01:57.804 --> 00:01:59.584
undergo intensive training

00:01:59.584 --> 00:02:02.474
inside an abandoned park in Mexico City.

00:02:02.474 --> 00:02:04.195
To prepare for the next earthquake,

00:02:04.195 --> 00:02:07.778
the Topos must stay in
peak physical shape.

00:02:09.114 --> 00:02:13.216
They also learn to identify
risks of collapsing buildings

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:16.049
and run simulated rescue missions.

00:02:18.458 --> 00:02:20.439
- [Narrator] The Topos are
so good at what they do

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:23.037
that they travel the world
helping other countries

00:02:23.037 --> 00:02:25.370
in their moments of despair.

00:02:38.425 --> 00:02:41.758
(mid-tempo piano music)

